# Supporting Non-Profit Organisations - Sipping for South Africa

Supporting Non-Profit Organisations like HPI (Humanatarian Projects International) is what we like to do at Rhythm Culture. We are donating two five week courses to a silent auction at the Sipping for South Africa event. Six USC students are creating an event on behalf of HPI (Humanatarian Projects International) as a part of a third year PR project. Funds raised will be going to the next HPI trip to South Africa to build four homes for orphan children. The HPI is a not for profit organisation that sends a team of volunteer workers to help relieve poverty and distress for orphans around the world. Trip can be short helping missions or long building missions. The event will be held at the Kawana Community Centre on May 21st 2015 from 6pm-9pm and the main focus of the event is wine tasting. [Book your place here](http://www.eventbrite.com.au/e/sipping-for-south-africa-tickets-16762844118?aff=SippingforSouthAfrica) [Facebook event](https://www.facebook.com/events/748087888644549/)
